M) components; and technical support services during installation and the transition to operations and maintenance. The company sells its products to engineering, procurement, and construction firms that build solar energy projects; utilities; solar developers, independent power producers; solar module manufacturers; and charge point operators. Shoals Technologies Group, Inc. was founded in 1996 and is headquartered in Portland, Tennessee.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Brandon  Moss | CEO & Director | Age 46 | Compensation: $1.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $321K ranks in the below the sector median among Technology peers, with revenue growing 22%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Shoals Technologies Group, Inc. is a small-cap technology business with a $1.3B market cap on $475M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +13% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, with gross margins sitting at 36%.","The company is burning through $16M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 5.6\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 276% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":2.760150633830604},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.5% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 9% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Technology ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (52% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Sector under pressure with a 18.0% decline over the past 6 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 10% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Technical Reactions to SHLS Trends in Macro Strategies","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/78/Technical_Reactions_to_SHLS_Trends_in_Macro_Strategies_112726072002_1795825202.html","date":"2026-11-28","timestamp":1795825202.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Are ZS, BILL, SHLS Obtaining Fair Deals for their Shareholders?","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/are-zs-bill-shls-o